    "cases": [
      "Five owners nested in a request containing records, a list, strings and an optional fallback.",
      "A duplicate owner late in an aggregate must fail after staging distinct owners. The guest checks the specific error, forces GC, proves every input still usable and then performs a valid transfer; the provider rejects any invalid request that reaches it.",
      "Responses cover a variant with tuple and optional owner list, the absent-list case, an owned result error, Unicode text and a payload-free variant.",
      "Eight pre-start compound transfers are held by provider backpressure; all five committed inputs are destroyed before cancellation acknowledgement.",
      "Eight suspended borrowed calls expire their borrow only after native cancellation acknowledges; late native completion fails.",
      "Eight ready-result races return successfully in the observed runs; the C caller validates values and destroys the returned owners.",
      "Eight deterministic unclaimed response cancellations: the provider prepares the response before suspension and returns it during CANCEL. Six carry 14 resource owners in total; two carry text or a payload-free variant. The generated C adapter discards the response without JS publication before acknowledging cancellation.",
      "Each call preserves an independent live sibling through acknowledgement, then completes it normally and reuses an idle Store with empty native gates.",
      "128 input resources, 32 sibling resources and 28 newly created result resources are each destroyed exactly once per run."
    ],
